# L8-LN: the past-131k ladder on Lever N + prefix reuse, audited (the strict ladder, concurrent equal to solo at about 140k and 253k with two or more seats past 131k together). READ: every concurrent text equals its
# solo text, zero audit mismatches, the matrix verdict PASS. The box is the gate's own worst case: the matrix plan re-runs both arms after a first divergence, so 2 arms x 2 runs x (5,400 + 120) s = 22,080 s = 368 minutes, and the serving gate refuses a plan that does not fit its box (measured from the gate step's start) before a container starts. The admit rule adds the 30 minutes the reset before it may take.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-2 window pack (tp4-w2-levern-jobs: Lever N robustness, then the cutover; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-audit-nolna
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,32768,140000,253920,16384,65536,200000,253000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
C2_GATE_JIT=record
C2_GATE_AUDITS=extent
C2_GATE_SALT=fresh
C2_BOX_MINUTES=368
